<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — Smooth AB Curve dialog (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual + behavioural PARITY reimplementation of the WinForms
    `Forms/Guidance/FormSmoothAB` (source: FormSmoothAB.cs + FormSmoothAB.Designer.cs). Per
    AAP §0.3.3 this is a faithful re-platform of the currently rendered Windows Forms surface,
    never a redesign: every size, position and font below is taken verbatim from
    FormSmoothAB.Designer.cs (WinForms pixels map 1:1 to Avalonia device-independent pixels at
    96 dpi; point font sizes are converted pt × 96/72 → DIP).

    The dialog lets the operator tune how strongly the active AB curve is smoothed. Holding the
    Up arrow raises a "smooth count" (clamped 2..100) and holding the Down arrow lowers it; each
    adjustment re-runs curve.SmoothAB(count × 2) and repaints the field. "For Now" applies the
    smoothing for the current session, "To File" also persists the tracks, and Cancel discards.

    CODE-BEHIND CONTRACT — FormSmoothABView.axaml.cs (partial class AgOpenGPS.Views.FormSmoothABView : Window):
      * This view is IMPERATIVE, not MVVM: there is intentionally NO x:DataType, no DataContext
        and no {Binding}. The x:Name'd controls below are the entire integration surface and keep
        their ORIGINAL WinForms names so the migrated code-behind addresses them exactly as
        FormSmoothAB.cs / FormSmoothAB.Designer.cs did. No event handlers are wired in this markup
        — the code-behind attaches them by name (reproducing the WinForms handlers), so the view
        compiles independently of whatever handler names the code-behind chooses:
          - btnNorth / btnSouth : RepeatButton (hold-to-repeat). The originals raised repeated
                                  MouseDown while held via AgLibrary.Controls.RepeatButton; the
                                  Avalonia built-in RepeatButton repeats Click while held (the
                                  parity match). btnNorth (Up) raises the count, btnSouth (Dn)
                                  lowers it; the code-behind calls curve.SmoothAB and updates
                                  lblSmooth + the main GL view per adjustment.
          - lblSmooth           : the large smooth-count readout. The WinForms Load handler set
                                  this to "**" (the design-time "99" is replaced at load); the
                                  code-behind reproduces that and writes the live count each nudge.
          - bntOK               : "For Now" — apply smoothing for the session and close.
          - btnSave             : "To File" — apply, persist tracks, and close.
          - btnCancel           : discard and close.
      * Caption text is assigned at runtime from gStr by the code-behind, exactly as the WinForms
        constructor did (this.Text = gStr.gsSmoothABCurve; bntOK.Text = gStr.gsForNow;
        btnSave.Text = gStr.gsToFile;). The literals below ("Smooth AB Curve" / "For Now" /
        "To File") are the Designer placeholders the code-behind overrides; because an Avalonia
        Button's caption lives inside its Content (here an Image-over-text stack, not a .Text
        property), the localisable captions are exposed as their own named TextBlocks
        (bntOKText / btnSaveText) following the sibling convention (see Pickers/* btnOpenText).

    WINDOW SHELL — mirrors FormSmoothAB.Designer.cs:
      Text "Smooth AB Curve"      -> Title (design-time literal; code-behind sets gStr.gsSmoothABCurve).
      ClientSize 231 x 393        -> root Canvas Width/Height 231 x 393 (absolute layout).
      BackColor WhiteSmoke        -> Background="WhiteSmoke". This dialog is a FIXED light surface,
                                     theme-independent (it was never part of FormGPS day/night
                                     SwapDayNightMode chrome), so it is NOT bound to AogFrameBrush
                                     and its text Foreground is hard-coded Black for legibility.
      ControlBox = false          -> [XPLAT] MINOR DEVIATION: Avalonia cannot hide only the
                                     close/min/max caption buttons. The no-control-box look is
                                     approximated by keeping the normal title bar
                                     (SystemDecorations="Full"); the dialog is dismissed via its own
                                     For Now / To File / Cancel buttons exactly as the WinForms form.
      FormBorderStyle (default)   -> the source did not set it (default Sizable), so the system
                                     decorations + caption are KEPT and CanResize="True".
      Width / Height 231 x 393    -> set explicitly per the assigned spec (same shell shape as the
                                     sibling FormEventViewerView: Full + resizable + explicit W/H).
                                     On platforms that draw native decorations outside the client
                                     (e.g. Windows), the client is exactly 231 x 393; where
                                     client-side decorations are used the title bar takes a few
                                     pixels — the documented minor deviation above, mitigated by
                                     CanResize="True".
      ShowInTaskbar = false       -> ShowInTaskbar="False".
      StartPosition CenterParent  -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner" (shown over FormGPS;
                                     replaces the WinForms ScreenHelper.IsOnScreen reposition, which
                                     CenterOwner makes unnecessary).
      Font Tahoma                 -> FontFamily="Tahoma"; children carry their point sizes converted
                                     to DIP (36pt -> 48, 14.25pt -> 19).

    Button glyphs are served from the GPS assembly (assembly name "AgOpenGPS") via avares:// URIs,
    mapped from the Designer's Image assignments (each asset confirmed native 64 x 64):
      btnSouth.Image = Resources.DnArrow64     -> btnImages/DnArrow64.png
      btnNorth.Image = Resources.UpArrow64     -> btnImages/UpArrow64.png
      bntOK.Image    = Resources.FileDontSave  -> btnImages/FileDontSave.png
      btnSave.Image  = Resources.FileSave      -> btnImages/FileSave.png
      btnCancel.Image= Resources.Cancel64      -> btnImages/Cancel64.png

    No System.Windows.Forms, no OpenTK.GLControl, no GMap, no ColorPicker types are referenced —
    Avalonia 11.3 markup only.
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.FormSmoothABView"
        Title="Smooth AB Curve"
        Width="231"
        Height="393"
        Background="{DynamicResource AogLegacyWhiteSmokeBrush}"
        SystemDecorations="Full"
        CanResize="True"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        FontFamily="Tahoma">

    <!--
        Flat, chrome-less push buttons reproduce the WinForms FlatStyle.Flat +
        FlatAppearance.BorderSize = 0 + UseVisualStyleBackColor face: just the scaled glyph (and,
        for bntOK / btnSave, a caption beneath it), with no button surface in any interaction
        state. Because Avalonia type selectors match the EXACT type (a RepeatButton is NOT matched
        by a "Button" selector), the style is declared once for Button and once for RepeatButton —
        the proven sibling convention (see Settings/FormSteerView.axaml). The :pointerover /
        :pressed template overrides suppress the Fluent hover/press fill that would otherwise box
        the glyph (the same technique used by FormYesView / FormPanView / FormSaveOrNotView).
    -->
    <Window.Styles>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>

        <Style Selector="RepeatButton.flatImage">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="RepeatButton.flatImage:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="RepeatButton.flatImage:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Styles>

    <!--
        Root Canvas == the WinForms client area (231 x 393). The six direct children are placed at
        their exact WinForms designer Location/Size via Canvas.Left / Canvas.Top, giving true pixel
        parity for this fixed-layout dialog.
    -->
    <Canvas Width="231" Height="393">

        <!-- ============================ adjust arrows ============================ -->

        <!-- btnSouth: WinForms AgLibrary.Controls.RepeatButton @ (33,12) 72 x 72, Image DnArrow64,
             FlatStyle.Flat + BorderSize 0. The Down arrow LOWERS the smooth count (btnSouth_MouseDown
             decrements smoothCount, clamped to a minimum of 2). Hold-to-repeat: Delay before the first auto-repeat and
             Interval between repeats are set to comfortable values so a press-and-hold steps the value,
             reproducing the source RepeatButton behaviour. The 64 x 64 glyph is centred in the 72 x 72
             button (≈ 4 px inset each side), matching the WinForms native-size Image draw. -->
        <RepeatButton x:Name="btnSouth"
                      Classes="flatImage"
                      Canvas.Left="33" Canvas.Top="12"
                      Width="72" Height="72"
                      Delay="300" Interval="100"
                      AutomationProperties.Name="Decrease smoothing">
            <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/DnArrow64.png"
                   Width="64" Height="64" Stretch="Uniform" />
        </RepeatButton>

        <!-- btnNorth: WinForms RepeatButton @ (130,12) 72 x 72, Image UpArrow64, FlatStyle.Flat +
             BorderSize 0. The Up arrow RAISES the smooth count (btnNorth_MouseDown: smoothCount++
             clamped to <= 100). Same hold-to-repeat cadence as btnSouth. -->
        <RepeatButton x:Name="btnNorth"
                      Classes="flatImage"
                      Canvas.Left="130" Canvas.Top="12"
                      Width="72" Height="72"
                      Delay="300" Interval="100"
                      AutomationProperties.Name="Increase smoothing">
            <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/UpArrow64.png"
                   Width="64" Height="64" Stretch="Uniform" />
        </RepeatButton>

        <!-- lblSmooth: WinForms Label @ (73,96), Tahoma 36pt Bold (-> 48 DIP), AutoSize, BackColor
             Transparent. The large smooth-count readout. Initial text "**" matches FormSmoothAB_Load
             (the designer's "99" was only a design-time placeholder). Foreground hard-coded Black for
             legibility on the fixed WhiteSmoke surface (theme-independent). Left auto-sized (no fixed
             Width) so it grows with the digit count exactly like the WinForms AutoSize label. -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="lblSmooth"
                   Canvas.Left="73" Canvas.Top="96"
                   FontFamily="Tahoma"
                   FontSize="48"
                   FontWeight="Bold"
                   Foreground="Black"
                   Text="**" />

        <!-- ============================ command buttons ============================ -->

        <!-- bntOK: WinForms Button @ (12,179) 93 x 93, FlatStyle.Flat + BorderSize 0, Image
             FileDontSave with ImageAlign TopCenter and Text "For Now" with TextAlign BottomCenter.
             "For Now" applies smoothing for the session and closes (bntOK_Click). The Image-over-text
             layout is reproduced with a centred vertical StackPanel (Image on top, caption beneath) —
             the sibling convention for in-button captions (see FormAgShareSettingsView). The caption
             is its own named TextBlock (bntOKText) so the code-behind can set gStr.gsForNow at runtime
             (an Avalonia Button has no .Text; the caption lives in Content). -->
        <Button x:Name="bntOK"
                Classes="flatImage"
                Canvas.Left="12" Canvas.Top="179"
                Width="93" Height="93"
                AutomationProperties.Name="For Now">
            <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center"
                        Spacing="2">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/FileDontSave.png"
                       Width="64" Height="64" Stretch="Uniform"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center" />
                <TextBlock x:Name="bntOKText"
                           Text="For Now"
                           FontFamily="Tahoma"
                           FontSize="19"
                           Foreground="Black"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                           TextAlignment="Center" />
            </StackPanel>
        </Button>

        <!-- btnSave: WinForms Button @ (130,179) 93 x 93, FlatStyle.Flat + BorderSize 0, Image
             FileSave (ImageAlign TopCenter) + Text "To File" (TextAlign BottomCenter). "To File"
             applies smoothing, persists the tracks, and closes (btnSave_Click). Same Image-over-caption
             layout as bntOK; caption exposed as btnSaveText for gStr.gsToFile localisation. -->
        <Button x:Name="btnSave"
                Classes="flatImage"
                Canvas.Left="130" Canvas.Top="179"
                Width="93" Height="93"
                AutomationProperties.Name="To File">
            <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center"
                        Spacing="2">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/FileSave.png"
                       Width="64" Height="64" Stretch="Uniform"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center" />
                <TextBlock x:Name="btnSaveText"
                           Text="To File"
                           FontFamily="Tahoma"
                           FontSize="19"
                           Foreground="Black"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                           TextAlignment="Center" />
            </StackPanel>
        </Button>

        <!-- btnCancel: WinForms Button @ (130,298) 93 x 82, FlatStyle.Flat + BorderSize 0, Image
             Cancel64. Image-ONLY (the source assigns no .Text to btnCancel). Discards the smoothing
             and closes (btnCancel_Click). The 64 x 64 glyph is centred in the 93 x 82 button. -->
        <Button x:Name="btnCancel"
                Classes="flatImage"
                Canvas.Left="130" Canvas.Top="298"
                Width="93" Height="82"
                AutomationProperties.Name="Cancel">
            <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/Cancel64.png"
                   Width="64" Height="64" Stretch="Uniform" />
        </Button>

    </Canvas>
</Window>
